Two :FINALLY clauses where the first is empty. single_finally fires on the
second :FINALLY; the statement after it belongs to no clause, so the first
:FINALLY is still reported as finally_empty (diag.single_finally,
diag.finally_empty fourth Flags fence).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE ReleaseLock;
	:PARAMETERS sLockName;
	:DECLARE bReleased;
	:TRY;
		bReleased := .T.;
	:FINALLY;
	:FINALLY;
		bReleased := .F.;
	:ENDTRY;
	:RETURN bReleased;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE ReleaseLock;
	:PARAMETERS sLockName;
	:DECLARE bReleased;

	:TRY;
		bReleased := .T.;
	:FINALLY;
	:FINALLY;
		bReleased := .F.;
	:ENDTRY;

	:RETURN bReleased;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
6:2-6:10 error finally_empty: ':FINALLY' must contain at least one statement
7:2-7:10 error single_finally: Only one ':FINALLY' block is allowed per ':TRY'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
2:14-2:23 hint unused_variable: Variable 'sLockName' is declared but never used
6:2-6:10 error finally_empty: ':FINALLY' must contain at least one statement
7:2-7:10 error single_finally: Only one ':FINALLY' block is allowed per ':TRY'
